{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-05-24T21:05:07.142Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command_1779656707142_1","parameters":{"description":"Creating papers/README.md to document the downloaded papers.","command":"cat > papers/README.md << 'EOF'\n# Downloaded Papers\n\n1. [A Novel Distributed PV Power Forecasting Approach Based on Time-LLM](2503.06216v1_A_Novel_Distributed_PV_Power_Forecasting_Approach_Based_on_Time-LLM.pdf)\n   - Authors: Huapeng Lin, Miao Yu\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: 2503.06216\n   - Why relevant: Applies Time-LLM to photovoltaic power forecasting, showing superiority in both short-term and long-term scenarios.\n\n2. [Evaluating LLMs on Real-World Forecasting Against Expert Forecasters](2507.04562v3_Evaluating_LLMs_on_Real-World_Forecasting_Against_Expert_Forecasters.pdf)\n   - Authors: Janna Lu\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: 2507.04562\n   - Why relevant: Directly compares LLMs against expert human forecasters on real-world questions (Metaculus).\n\n3. [Pitfalls in Evaluating Language Model Forecasters](2506.00723v1_Pitfalls_in_Evaluating_Language_Model_Forecasters.pdf)\n   - Authors: Daniel Paleka, Shashwat Goel, Jonas Geiping, F. Tramèr\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: 2506.00723\n   - Why relevant: Critically examines the claims of LLM forecasting superiority and identifies issues like temporal leakage.\n\n4. [ForecastBench: A Dynamic Benchmark of AI Forecasting Capabilities](2409.19839v5_ForecastBench_A_Dynamic_Benchmark_of_AI_Forecasting_Capabilities.pdf)\n   - Authors: Ezra Karger et al.\n   - Year: 2024\n   - arXiv: 2409.19839\n   - Why relevant: Provides a benchmark comparing LLMs, human experts, and the general public on future events.\n\n5. [MTBench: A Multimodal Time Series Benchmark for Temporal Reasoning and Question Answering](2503.16858v2_MTBench_A_Multimodal_Time_Series_Benchmark_for_Temporal_Reasoning_and_Question_Answering.pdf)\n   - Authors: Jialin Chen et al.\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: 2503.16858\n   - Why relevant: Benchmark for multimodal (text + time series) forecasting.\n\n6. [How AI Forecasts AI Jobs: Benchmarking LLM Predictions of Labor Market Changes](2510.23358v1_How_AI_Forecasts_AI_Jobs_Benchmarking_LLM_Predictions_of_Labor_Market_Changes.pdf)\n   - Authors: Sheri Osborn et al.\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: 2510.23358\n   - Why relevant: Evaluates LLM predictions on labor market changes, comparing short-term vs long-term horizons.\n\n7. [Logo-LLM: Local and Global Modeling with Large Language Models for Time Series Forecasting](2505.11017v2_Logo-LLM_Local_and_Global_Modeling_with_Large_Language_Models_for_Time_Series_Forecasting.pdf)\n   - Authors: Wenjie Ou et al.\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: 2505.11017\n   - Why relevant: Proposes a framework for capturing both local patterns (short-term) and global dependencies (long-term).\n\n8. [Time-LLM: Time Series Forecasting by Reprogramming Large Language Models](2310.01728v2_Time-LLM_Time_Series_Forecasting_by_Reprogramming_Large_Language_Models.pdf)\n   - Authors: Ming Jin et al.\n   - Year: 2023\n   - arXiv: 2310.01728\n   - Why relevant: Foundational paper for using LLMs for time series forecasting.\n\n9. [One Fits All: Power General Time Series Analysis by Pretrained LM](2303.14295v1_One_Fits_All_Power_General_Time_Series_Analysis_by_Pretrained_LM.pdf)\n   - Authors: Tian Zhou et al.\n   - Year: 2023\n   - arXiv: 2303.14295\n   - Why relevant: Early influential work on using frozen LLMs for time series analysis (OFM).\nEOF\n"}}
