{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-05-24T21:08:01.911Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command_1779656881911_0","parameters":{"command":"cat > datasets/README.md << 'EOF'\n# Downloaded Datasets\n\nThis directory contains datasets for the research project. Data files are NOT committed to git due to size.\n\n## Dataset 1: ForecastBench\n- **Source**: [forecastingresearch/forecastbench-datasets](https://huggingface.co/datasets/forecastingresearch/forecastbench-datasets)\n- **Type**: Event-based forecasting (Long-term Low-data)\n- **Contents**: \n  - `forecast_sets/`: Periodic snapshots of questions and forecasts.\n  - `human_forecasts/`: Data from expert and public forecasters.\n  - `llm_forecasts/`: Data from various LLMs.\n- **Usage**: Used to compare LLMs against human experts on real-world future events.\n\n## Dataset 2: ETTm1 (Electricity Transformer Temperature)\n- **Source**: [ts-arena/ettm1](https://huggingface.co/datasets/ts-arena/ettm1)\n- **Type**: Numerical time series (Short-term High-data)\n- **Frequency**: 15 minutes\n- **Features**: 6 power load features + Oil Temperature (OT)\n- **Usage**: Standard benchmark for numerical time series forecasting models like Time-LLM.\n\n## Setup Instructions\nThe ForecastBench dataset was cloned using git-lfs. To update or re-download:\n```bash\ngit clone https://huggingface.co/datasets/forecastingresearch/forecastbench-datasets datasets/forecastbench\n```\n\nThe ETTm1 dataset was downloaded via the HuggingFace `datasets` library and saved as CSVs.\nEOF\n\ncat > datasets/.gitignore << 'EOF'\n# Exclude large data files\n*.csv\n*.json\n*.jsonl\n*.parquet\nforecastbench/\nts/\nEOF\n","description":"Creating datasets/README.md and datasets/.gitignore."}}
