{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-05-24T21:08:50.805Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command_1779656930805_0","parameters":{"description":"Creating the resources.md file.","command":"cat > resources.md << 'EOF'\n# Resources Catalog: LLMs and Forecasting\n\n## Summary\nThis document catalogs all resources gathered for the research project, including papers, datasets, and code repositories.\n\n## Papers\nTotal papers downloaded: 9\n\n| Title | Year | arXiv | Key Info |\n|-------|------|-------|----------|\n| Time-LLM | 2024 | 2310.01728 | Foundational for TS-LLM |\n| ForecastBench | 2025 | 2409.19839 | Primary evaluation benchmark |\n| Evaluating LLMs... | 2025 | 2507.04562 | LLM vs Expert comparison |\n| Pitfalls in Evaluation | 2025 | 2506.00723 | Critical view on contamination |\n| Logo-LLM | 2025 | 2505.11017 | Local/Global modeling |\n| One Fits All | 2023 | 2303.14295 | Early TS-LLM work |\n| MTBench | 2025 | 2503.16858 | Multimodal benchmark |\n| How AI Forecasts AI Jobs | 2025 | 2510.23358 | Market impact study |\n| Distributed PV Power | 2025 | 2503.06216 | Domain-specific application |\n\n## Datasets\nTotal datasets downloaded: 2\n\n| Name | Source | Type | Location |\n|------|--------|------|----------|\n| ForecastBench | HF | Event-based | `datasets/forecastbench/` |\n| ETTm1 | HF | Time Series | `datasets/ts/` |\n\n## Code Repositories\nTotal repositories cloned: 4\n\n| Name | Purpose | Location |\n|------|---------|----------|\n| Time-LLM | TS Reprogramming | `code/Time-LLM/` |\n| ForecastBench | Evaluation | `code/forecastbench/` |\n| Logo-LLM | Local/Global TS | `code/Logo-LLM/` |\n| One-Fits-All | Foundation TS | `code/One-Fits-All/` |\n\n## Recommendations for Experiment Design\n\n1. **Short-term High-data**: Evaluate Time-LLM on ETTm1. Focus on how LLMs handle high-frequency data compared to statistical baselines (ARIMA/LSTM).\n2. **Long-term Low-data**: Analyze ForecastBench human vs LLM scores. Specifically look at \"long-term\" questions (e.g., > 1 year) to see if LLMs have an advantage in long-horizon reasoning.\n3. **Cross-Domain Verification**: Test if an LLM trained on event forecasting (ForecastBench) can help improve numerical forecasting (Time-LLM) through better \"context\" integration.\nEOF\n"}}
